            <ArticleTitle>[Creation of expert centers on endometriosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1218-1222</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0755-4982(17)30445-1</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.lpm.2017.09.023</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endometriosis is a frequent pathology with a high incidence of deep infiltrating endometriosis and complex forms that can affect 20% of patients with endometriosis. The incidence of infertility associated with endometriosis can reach 50%. The complexity of care requires the creation of expert centers working in networks with general practitioners. Criteria for defining these expert centers are being drawn up, based on structural criteria (multidisciplinary consultation meeting), links with medical assistance structures for procreation and activity criteria for severe and complex forms (number of interventions per center and per surgeon).</AbstractText>
